      ro: "Raleigh, capitala statului Carolina de Nord, a fost fondata ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n 1792 special pentru a servi drept scaun al guvernului statal, fiind numita ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n onoarea exploratorului Sir Walter Raleigh. Cunoscut ca ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½Ora?ul StejarilorÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ datorita abunden?ei acestor arbori ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n centrul istoric, metropola s-a transformat dintr-un centru agricol modest ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ntr-un lider tehnologic global. Raleigh formeaza, alaturi de Durham ?i Chapel Hill, renumitul Research Triangle Park (ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nfiin?at ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n 1959), cel mai mare parc de cercetare ?tiin?ifica din Statele Unite. Acest cluster atrage sute de companii de biotehnologie, inginerie ?i informatica, consolidÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nd o economie moderna vibranta. Pe lÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nga inovație, orașul gazduiește Universitatea de Stat din Carolina de Nord (fondata ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n 1887), care alimenteaza continuu pia?a muncii cu forța de munca ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nalt calificata. Geografie K8 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ inovație tehnologica ?i poluri economice.",
      en: "Raleigh is the capital city of North Carolina and one of the fastest-growing cities in the United States. Often referred to as the 'City of Oaks' due to its extensive oak tree canopy, Raleigh is geographically situated in the Piedmont region. Its economy is overwhelmingly driven by its proximity to the Research Triangle Park (RTP), one of the largest and most prominent high-tech research and development parks in the country. The presence of major universitiesÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½including North Carolina State University within the city, and nearby Duke University and UNC Chapel HillÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½fosters a highly educated workforce that sustains massive biotechnology, pharmaceutical, and technology sectors. The city was meticulously planned in 1792 specifically to serve as the state capital. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ research clusters and planned capitals."
