      en: "Stockton is a major city located in the Central Valley of California, situated along the San Joaquin River. Historically, it developed as a critical supply and transportation center during the California Gold Rush, uniquely functioning as an inland deep-water port, a status it maintains today through a dredged channel connecting it to the San Francisco Bay. This port facility makes Stockton a vital logistical hub for exporting the immense agricultural output of the surrounding San Joaquin Valley to international markets. In recent decades, Stockton has experienced significant economic challenges and was heavily impacted by the 2008 subprime mortgage crisis, leading to a highly publicized municipal bankruptcy in 2012, from which it has since emerged and restructured. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ inland ports and agricultural logistics."
