      ro: "Buffalo este situat la grani?a de nord-vest a statului New York, chiar la sursa rÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ului Niagara, la punctul estic de scurgere din masivul Lac Erie. Importan?a sa unica deriva din construirea epocala a Canalului Erie, finalizat complet ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n anul 1825. Acel drum pe apa a legat direct Oceanul Atlantic (prin fluviul Hudson) de Marile Lacuri, transformÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nd miraculos a?ezarea frontaliera Buffalo ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n al optulea cel mai uria? ?i mai bogat ora? american la intrarea ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n anii 1900. CÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½?tigÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nd titulatura de ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½Ora?ul LuminiiÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ (City of Light), a fost primul metroul american dotat pe scara larga cu iluminat public, generat tocmai din captarea hidroelectrica a Cascadei Niagara aflate ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n preajma (1896). Reculul greu al economiei industriale dupa anii 1950 a dus la declin, dar peisajul lui reÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nvie astazi, protejÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nd o incredibila varietate din primele modele de zgÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½rie-nori naționali. Istorie K8 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ rolul strategic al canalelor navigabile.",
      en: "Buffalo is the second-largest city in New York state, located at the eastern end of Lake Erie, adjacent to the Canadian border and near Niagara Falls. Historically, Buffalo was an industrial titan; the opening of the Erie Canal in 1825 transformed it into the primary gateway for commerce between the East Coast and the expanding Midwest. The city capitalized on its position by developing massive grain elevators, steel mills, and automobile manufacturing plants. Like many Rust Belt cities, Buffalo faced severe economic decline in the late 20th century. However, recent revitalization efforts have focused on healthcare, education, and leveraging its architectural heritage, which includes significant works by Frank Lloyd Wright and Louis Sullivan, alongside a distinct local culture famous for the invention of Buffalo wings. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ Great Lakes ports and Erie Canal history."
