      ro: "Rochester, situat pe malul sudic al Lacului Ontario ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n vestul statului New York, a fost unul dintre primele ora?e industriale de succes (boomtown) din America, crescÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nd spectaculos odata cu deschiderea Canalului Erie. La ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nceputul secolului al XIX-lea, mul?imea sa de mori de faina propulsate de cascadele rÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ului Genesee i-au adus titlul de ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½Ora?ul Morilor de FainaÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½. Ulterior, datorita uria?elor pepiniere de plante, a fost supranumit ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½Ora?ul FlorilorÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½. Mo?tenirea sa globala este ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nsa ancorata ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n inventica: aici, George Eastman a fondat celebra companie Kodak ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n 1888, transformÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nd orașul ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n centrul mondial al fotografiei. De asemenea, a fost baza de operațiuni a liderului aboli?ionist Frederick Douglass ?i a faimoasei activiste pentru drepturile femeilor Susan B. Anthony (care a votat ilegal aici ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n 1872). Astazi, tehnologia optica ?i universita?ile ramÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n piloni economici esențiali. Istorie K8 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ aboli?ionismul ?i mi?carea sufragetelor.",
      en: "Rochester is a prominent city in western New York, located on the southern shore of Lake Ontario at the mouth of the Genesee River. The city's early prosperity was driven by the numerous waterfalls on the Genesee, which powered massive flour mills, earning it the nickname 'The Flour City'. In the late 19th and 20th centuries, Rochester transformed into a global hub for technological innovation and precision manufacturing, serving as the birthplace and headquarters for giants like Eastman Kodak, Bausch & Lomb, and Xerox. While facing significant challenges due to the decline of traditional film photography and manufacturing, the city has leveraged its highly skilled workforce and institutions like the Rochester Institute of Technology (RIT) and the University of Rochester to transition toward optics, photonics, and biotechnology. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ technological transitions and Great Lakes geography."
