      ro: "Jackson, amplasat pe cursul pașnic al rÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ului Pearl, este capitala ?i cea mai mare metropola a statului Mississippi. Orașul a fost fondat la un deceniu dupa formarea statului (1821) pe un vechi avanpost de tranzac?ii numit LeFleur's Bluff, luÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nd ulterior numele controversatului erou militar ?i președinte Andrew Jackson. La fel ca alte ora?e din sud, a fost incendiat aproape complet de forțele lui Sherman ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n 1863 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n timpul Razboiului Civil, dobÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ndind denumirea sumbra de ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½Hornul ora?uluiÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ (Chimneyville) pentru singurele ruine ramase ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n picioare. Istoria recenta ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½l consacra pe fondul mi?carii acerbe pentru drepturile civile afro-americane din anii 1960. Orașul are onoarea de a deține singurul vulcan stins existent chiar sub limitele unei capitale americane, Jackson Volcano. Istorie K8 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ segregare, activi?ti civili ?i reforme (Medgar Evers).",
      en: "Jackson is the capital and most populous city of Mississippi, situated on the Pearl River in the south-central portion of the state. Established in 1821, the city was named in honor of General Andrew Jackson and explicitly planned in a grid pattern by architect Peter Vandorn to serve as the new state capital. Jackson played a profound and deeply turbulent role during the American Civil Rights Movement, marked by intense protests, sit-ins, and the tragic 1963 assassination of civil rights leader Medgar Evers. The city's rich cultural heritage is heavily defined by its contributions to blues, gospel, and soul music, earning it the moniker 'The City with Soul'. Today, the economy relies heavily on state administration, manufacturing, and healthcare. History K8 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ the Civil Rights Movement and musical heritage."
