      ro: "Hartford troneaza autoritar ca inima administrativa a statului Connecticut, instalata fix la mijlocul albiei de scurgere al rÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ului omonim. Descoperirile comerciale olandeze originare (1623) au dat drumul patrunderii exploratorului pastor britanic Thomas Hooker (ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n 1636). Influen?a istorica este masiva din simplul motiv ca locuitorii din Hartford ?i din alte colonii limitrofe au pus imediat la punct setul documentar Fundamental Orders of Connecticut (1639), tratat privit public de comunitatea americana drept prim-modelul veritabil absolut al unei Constitu?ii Occidentale funcționale. Secolele 19 ?i 20 au ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nclinat puterea totala la nivel corporativ, metropola fiind botezata pe buna dreptate global ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½Capitala Mondiala a AsigurarilorÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ (The Insurance Capital of the World), cu gigan?i faimo?i stabili?i permanent de foarte mult timp (ca spre exemplu grupul The Hartford ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n anul 1810). Istorie K8 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ actele constituționale primordiale timpurii.",
      en: "Hartford is the capital of Connecticut, located along the Connecticut River in the central part of the state. Historically one of the wealthiest cities in the United States following the Civil War, Hartford earned the moniker 'Insurance Capital of the World' due to the massive concentration of major insurance companies headquartered there, a legacy that continues to define its modern economy. The city is also deeply associated with literary history; it was the longtime residence of author Mark Twain, whose incredibly ornate Victorian Gothic home remains a major tourist destination. Despite facing modern urban challenges, Hartford maintains a robust corporate sector, significant historical architecture, and prominent cultural institutions like the Wadsworth Atheneum Museum of Art. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ corporate headquarters and specialized regional economies."
