      en: "Savannah is the oldest city in Georgia and a highly significant coastal seaport on the Savannah River. Established in 1733 by General James Oglethorpe, the city is internationally renowned for its unique, meticulously preserved original town plan, featuring an extensive grid interspersed with 22 shaded public squares draped in Spanish moss. Historically, Savannah generated immense wealth through the export of cotton and rice, supported by an enslaved workforce. Spared from destruction during the Civil War, its massive collection of antebellum architecture makes it one of the premier historical tourism destinations in the country. Simultaneously, the modern Port of Savannah is a massive economic engine, ranking among the busiest container ports in North America. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ colonial urban planning and coastal ports."
