      ro: "Concord vegheaza calm pur masiv ca structura pur guvernamentala la margine din fluviul Merrimack ?i e stabilit administrativ scaun de stat capitala din uria? muntos ?i natural stat New Hampshire. Fondata sub masiv conflict disputat la un vechi an clar fix pe marginea unei faimoase dispute pur teritoriale pe linia coloniei (1725, cunoscut la acea ora cu apelativ Penacook), a fost denumita oficial ?i final ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n a?ezamÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½nt sub faimosul ?i simbolic nume ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ConcordÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ abia tÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½rziu chiar ca semn de final de dispute ?i armonie finalizata curat pe 1765. Se afirma ca industria de greu calibru de mare tradiție pe domeniu absolut al granitelor dure s-a ridicat complet de aici pe ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ntreg teritoriu național, acest pur piatra a?ezata fiind ridicat formal fix la enormul faimos colosal edificiu pe național cladirea enorma la pur de biblioteca mare publica național americana ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n capitala pur mama Washington DC. Guvernul ?i sediul din inima orașului adapostește complet cea de a pur cea mai batrÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½na pur structura de sala de camere legislative pastrata oficial ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n continuu pe spațiul cu uz chiar de stat de State Unite formidabil neÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ntrerupt completat chiar pe anul curat 1819. Istorie K8 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ rolul pietrei (granit) ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½n urbanizarea americana.",
      en: "Concord is the capital city of New Hampshire, situated centrally within the state along the Merrimack River. Originally established as a plantation known as Penacook in 1725, it was strategically chosen as the state capital in 1808 due to its central location. Historically, Concord gained international fame during the 19th century for the massive production of 'Concord coaches', robust stagecoaches utilized extensively during American westward expansion. The city was also renowned for its high-quality granite quarries, which supplied stone for the Library of Congress. Today, Concord's economy relies heavily on state government, healthcare, and insurance, while its historic downtown retains much of its 19th-century red-brick commercial architecture. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ state capitals and historical manufacturing."
