      en: "Charleston is the capital and most populous city of West Virginia, located at the confluence of the Elk and Kanawha Rivers in the western foothills of the Appalachian Mountains. Historically, the city's early economy was built on the extraction of salt, and later heavily transitioned to coal, timber, and the massive production of chemicals, fueled by the region's abundant natural gas and brine deposits. While heavy industry and chemical manufacturing remain present along the Kanawha River Valley, the modern economy of Charleston is heavily reliant on state government operations, healthcare, and education. The city features the West Virginia State Capitol, renowned for its brilliant 293-foot gold dome, and serves as a cultural hub for the mountainous state. Geography K7 ÃƒÂ¯ÂÂ¿ÂÂ½ Appalachian settlements and resource extraction."
